  "section_notes": "The final text relaxes the S2 permanent failure cap to 7% with no mandatory sales stop above it, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 drops the mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 in favour of a regulator-discretion corrective-action path with no bounded window, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9). S3 keeps a 6-year retrofit window (Northwind's 38% coverage) and S4 sets suppression at 36 months (Halcyon's cost concern), so each company gains on different sections. Ambiguity: S2 'per-model results' to customers is read as numeric rates, which should be confirmed."
